			],
			"Message": "refactor(Cocoon): Enhance VS Code shim with structural methods and singular provider names\n\nImprove the VS Code Position and Range shims passed to language providers with structural methods that extensions expect:\n- Position now has isBefore/isBeforeOrEqual/isAfter/isAfterOrEqual/isEqual/compareTo/translate/with/toString\n- Range now has isEmpty/isSingleLine/contains/isEqual/intersection/union/with\n\nAdd proper language ID detection based on file extension mapping (rs→rust, ts/tsx→typescript, js/jsx→javascript, json/toml/md/py/go→respective languages).\n\nEnhance TextDocument shim with missing members: uri scheme/path, fileName without file:// prefix, isClosed, eol, proper lineAt handling for position objects, and save method.\n\nAdd support for singular method name variants that Mountain sends ($provideCompletion, $provideCodeAction, $provideDocumentHighlight, $provideDocumentSymbol, $provideWorkspaceSymbol, $provideDocumentFormatting, $provideDocumentRangeFormatting, $provideRename, $provideFoldingRange, $provideInlayHint, $provideCodeLens) in addition to the plural forms.\n\nThis ensures VS Code extensions that rely on Position/Range structural methods and various provider method names work correctly with the Cocoon language provider registry.",
			"SHA": "fd7d391a88fdc9e5ec80574416f47650325fa1d7"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-06T07:38:41Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				275,
				3
			],
			"Message": "feat(Cocoon): Implement language provider registry and $provide* method routing\n\nAdd a shared LanguageProviderRegistry singleton module that maps numeric provider handles to VS Code extension language provider objects. This registry is populated by APIFactoryService when extensions register providers (via registerHoverProvider, registerCompletionItemProvider, etc.) and queried by GRPCServerService when Mountain invokes providers via gRPC.\n\nUpdate IsValidMethod in GRPCServerService to accept $provide* method names (e.g., $provideHover, $provideCompletions) in addition to the standard \"service.method\" format. Add InvokeLanguageProvider to handle 14 language feature methods:\n\n- $provideHover: Converts VS Code Hover with markdown contents to DTO\n- $provideCompletions: Maps CompletionItem suggestions with label/kind/detail\n- $provideDefinition: Returns Location[] with normalized URI and range\n- $provideReferences: Returns reference locations with includeDeclaration\n- $provideCodeActions: Passes through code action requests\n- $provideDocumentHighlights: Returns document highlight locations\n- $provideDocumentSymbols: Returns hierarchical document symbols\n- $provideWorkspaceSymbols: Searches workspace symbols by query\n- $provideDocumentFormattingEdits / $provideDocumentRangeFormattingEdits\n- $provideSignatureHelp: Context-aware signature support\n- $provideRenameEdits: Rename with tracked edits\n- $provideFoldingRanges: Document folding regions\n- $provideInlayHints: Inline editor hints\n- $provideCodeLenses: Editor code lens indicators\n\nEach provider receives a minimal VS Code TextDocument shim with uri, fileName, languageId, and stub methods. Results are normalized from VS Code format to Mountain DTO format (RangeDTO, LocationDTO, CompletionListDTO, etc.).\n\nThis completes the language intelligence IPC loop: Sky requests feature → Mountain calls gRPC → Cocoon invokes provider → result returns to Sky → Monaco displays.",
			"SHA": "4e1316c6c2d11a32a4c0a74dc5990c87f9f7be18"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-06T06:32:35Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				274,
				1
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Cocoon): Format WorkspaceService and enhance TextDocument methods\n\nReformat Workspace.ts for consistent multi-line style and improve TextDocument interface implementations:\n- Format folder mapping, readFile call, ExtMap, and method implementations\n- Fix ternary handling for folder name extraction from string vs object\n- Improve getText() range handling with proper line slicing\n- Fix lineAt() to handle position objects correctly (not just line numbers)\n- Add offsetAt() implementation converting position to character offset\n- Add positionAt() implementation converting offset back to line/character\n- Add validateRange() to return range as-is (identity validation)\n- Add getWordRangeAtPosition() returning undefined\n\nThese refinements complete the TextDocument service interface with proper line/offset bidirectional conversion methods.",
			"SHA": "4117d5c9b9e8519c43f5fab4648c6e69032becca"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-06T04:14:00Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				274,
				2
			],
			"Message": "feat(Cocoon): Implement message dialog item selection and real document loading\n\nEnhance Window service message dialogs (showInformationMessage, showWarningMessage, showErrorMessage) to properly handle the items parameter by sending gRPC requests with items to Mountain and returning the selected item from the response.\n\nEnhance Workspace service openTextDocument to fetch actual file content from Mountain via fs.readFile instead of returning mock data. Implement full TextDocument interface with proper getText(range), lineAt, offsetAt, positionAt, validateRange, validatePosition methods. Add language detection based on file extension mapping.\n\nAlso add workspace folder DTO conversion to VSCode.WorkspaceFolder objects in AcceptWorkspaceData handler. Remove stale TODO comments about event stream emitters and WorkspaceConfiguration that have been addressed.\n\nThese changes complete the basic document opening flow, enabling real file content to be displayed in the editor with proper language detection.",
			"SHA": "9d2577507d57c5a63c5252240ddabb24c0e3e747"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-06T04:08:29Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				274,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Cocoon): Implement webview IPC notifications to Mountain\n\nReplace TODO placeholder implementations in WindowService's IPC proxy with actual gRPC notifications to Mountain backend. SendNotification now posts messages to the webview panel via webview.postMessage, SendRequest returns undefined as it's fire-and-forget (Sky resolves via onDidReceiveMessage), and the dispose callback notifies Mountain to destroy the webview panel via webview.dispose.\n\nThis completes the webview lifecycle IPC integration, enabling Cocoon to properly communicate panel state changes to Mountain.",
			"SHA": "7461ad28e3ff0c40a92feb6556104465e6503f6e"
		}
	],
